.\" man/man3/Docv::CrystalPages.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::CrystalPages" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CrystalPages \- Man pages for a Crystal shard (\fB\%docv \%gen\-cr\fR): \fB\%README.md\fR and the API doc comments, read through \fB\%crystal \%docs \%\-\-format \%json\fR, rendered as man(7) roff.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::CrystalPages\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Man pages for a Crystal shard (\fB\%docv \%gen\-cr\fR): \fB\%README.md\fR and the API
doc comments, read through \fB\%crystal \%docs \%\-\-format \%json\fR, rendered as
man(7) roff. One section 3 page per type (\fB\%Foo::Bar.3cr\fR), a page for
the top level when it declares anything, and a section 7 overview named
after the shard. Markdown goes through markd (\fB\%Markdown.tree\fR).
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
root = Docv::CrystalPages::Shard.root(Dir.current) || abort "not in a shard"
puts Docv::CrystalPages.generate(root, File.join(root, "man"))
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBGENERATED\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
GENERATED = "from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing."
.EE
.RE
.RE
.TP 4
\fBGENERATOR = "docv gen\-cr"\fR
Name of this generator, written into every page it generates.
.TP 4
\fBMARKER = "Generated by #{GENERATOR}"\fR
Comment text that marks a generated page. Only pages carrying it are
replaced or removed; pages of other generators that say the same
count too.
.TP 4
\fBOUTPUT = "man"\fR
The default output directory, relative to the shard root.
.PP
\fBOVERVIEW_SECTION = "7"\fR
.TP 4
\fBSUFFIX = "cr"\fR
Page name suffix after the section number (\fB\%Foo.3cr\fR), so the pages
never shadow C library pages.
.TP 4
\fBTYPE_SECTION = "3"\fR
Manual section of the type pages and of the overview page.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.base_name(full_name : String) : String\fR
Type path without generic arguments: \fB\%Foo(K, \%V)::Bar(T)\fR becomes
\fB\%Foo::Bar\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.blocks(text : String | Nil) : Array(Markd::Node)\fR
The markd blocks of a doc comment or README: \fB\%:showdoc:\fR, surrounding
whitespace and HTML without text (comments) dropped, adjacent text
nodes merged (markd splits text at \fB\%:\fR and other characters).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.children(node : Markd::Node) : Array(Markd::Node)\fR
The child nodes of \fInode\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.clean_type(text : String) : String\fR
Type names without the global \fB\%::\fR prefix the doc generator adds to
some return types.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.code_block(text : String) : Markd::Node\fR
A code block node holding \fItext\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.generate(root : String, output : String) : String\fR
Renders the pages of the shard in \fIroot\fR into \fIoutput\fR; returns a
report line.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.plain(node : Markd::Node) : String\fR
The text of \fInode\fR without markup, line breaks as spaces.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.summary(markdown : String | Nil) : String\fR
First sentence of the first paragraph of \fImarkdown\fR, by the rule of the
HTML doc generator.
